# Prerequisites
*.d

# Object files
*.o
*.ko
*.obj
*.elf

# Linker output
*.ilk
*.map
*.exp

# Precompiled Headers
*.gch
*.pch

# Libraries
*.lib
*.a
*.la
*.lo

# Shared objects (inc. Windows DLLs)
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib

# Executables
*.exe
*.out
*.app
*.i*86
*.x86_64
*.hex

# Debug files
*.dSYM/
*.su
*.idb
*.pdb

# Kernel Module Compile Results
*.mod*
*.cmd
.tmp_versions/
modules.order
Module.symvers
Mkfile.old
dkms.conf

# All west build directories live under build/ — ignore the contents,
# keep the folder itself (via .gitkeep) so the layout is preserved.
/build/*
!/build/.gitkeep

# ESP-IDF builds into its own in-app directory. The app moved under archived/
# when the ESP32 firmware was superseded by the standalone HealthyBridge repo;
# keep both paths ignored so a stale build tree can't be committed by accident.
/app_esp32c6_esp_idf/build
/archived/app_esp32c6_esp_idf/build

/CMakeFiles
CMakeCache.txt

# macOS Finder metadata
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Python host tools (tools/healthypi, tools/smpgroup)
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
# sdist/wheel staging. The /build/* rule above is anchored to the repo
# root, so it does NOT cover these -- `pip wheel tools/healthypi` drops a
# full copy of the sources under tools/<pkg>/build/lib/ and it was staged
# for commit once before this rule existed.
tools/*/build/
tools/*/dist/

# --- never published -------------------------------------------------------
# Internal working notes: plans, handoffs, phase trackers, bring-up and debug
# logs, roadmaps, the factory SOP and assistant working notes. They are kept
# locally and archived in the private reference repository, but they go stale
# within a week of any publish and describe commercial sequencing and defect
# history, so they are not part of the published tree. Do not un-ignore them.
/docs/internal/
/CLAUDE.md

# ST Edge AI tool output (console logs, ONNX/JSON intermediates, the .raw weight
# blob) used to be ignored here. Those rules moved on 2026-08-31 with the
# compute-module firmware, to Protocentral/healthylink-compute-fw. Nothing in
# this repository runs ST Edge AI or generates its byproducts any more; if you
# find yourself wanting these rules back, the code they belong to is in the
# other repository.
